Backstory: Rhea's family treated her first projection as a medical emergency, which was reasonable: a child who appears unconscious while describing the ceiling from above is frightening. Years of testing found nothing mundane that explained it. Lunaris eventually connected the episodes to astral magic and taught her to return deliberately, shorten sessions, and protect her resting body. She became one of the strongest student advocates for privacy rules because her own power makes boundary violations unusually easy. At school she works closely with Cassia Moonvale in the Dreamweavers Guild, but their abilities are distinct: Cassia moves through dreams, while Rhea travels astrally through the waking magical environment. She helps guide meditations before some full-moon and Wildering Woods activities and can serve as a supervised route observer during Moonlit Challenges. Rhea enjoys Pineharbor because its mundane streets feel pleasantly quiet in the astral sense, though she follows school rules and never projects through private homes. Her long-term growth centers on learning that being able to leave a difficult situation spiritually does not mean she should leave emotionally.

