Backstory: Aris was one of the original faculty voices pushing Lunaris to teach ordinary mathematics, science, literature, civics, and history alongside supernatural subjects. He rejected the idea that magical students should be educated only for magical communities. During the New Moon transition, his meticulous records helped expose outdated policies and prove that mixed-species classes had better outcomes than isolated tracks. His classroom is now a core meeting point for every kind of student: werewolves analyzing population statistics beside portal weavers studying geography, Beastweres debating personhood law beside cryomancers discussing thermodynamics. He is stern about evidence but equally stern that a person's species is never evidence of their character.

